// test (ball.px/ball.py -> current position) catches fast balls that would
// otherwise tunnel through a brick in one step; a discrete fallback catches a
// ball already resting inside one (sticky case). At most ONE velocity flip per
// axis per pass, so a ball straddling a seam between two bricks never gets its
// two flips cancelled. Returns the number of bricks broken.
